    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'TETRIS

    Release year: 1984


    In Tetris, a player controls a set
    of falling blocks to attempt to form rows as they stack them. If a row is formed,
    it disappears and the player gains points. The player would gain more points
    for making multiple rows at once - and can make up to 4 rows using the fabled
    line piece!


    Tetris still has a thriving competetive scene. With the game
    being out for so long, it has been optimized to the point where players are restricted
    only by the hardware they play on! After a technique was developed where players
    tapped the *back* of their controllers to move blocks faster, they needed to
    modify the original game to make it hard enough to stop the best of the best.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 390c06d404a51b047afaaca45f7c13c6, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6740465015241546099, guid: 390c06d404a51b047afaaca45f7c13c6, type: 2}
